Synthetic content
-----------------

Every operation fixture published by this project is fully synthetic. Actors,
identifiers, amounts, dates, addresses, documents, messages, thresholds,
policies and event plans were invented for the benchmark.

The fixtures are informed by operational topology of the kind found in the
domains they model. They transfer semantic structure and failure modes only.
They contain no production code, customer records, contacts, addresses,
proprietary message text, internal prices or real operational thresholds.

**No fixture is Dwelly policy.** No fixture describes how Dwelly, or any other
organisation, actually operates, and no fixture should be read as a statement of
anyone's real workflow, threshold or approval rule.


Historical components
---------------------

OperateBench incorporates methodology and infrastructure from BoundaryBench, the
predecessor project, as the foundation of the OperateBench Boundary Track.
BoundaryBench artifacts retain their original names, identifiers and digests,
and are cited as "BoundaryBench evidence, reused by the OperateBench Boundary
Track". OperateBench is not a rename of BoundaryBench, and no BoundaryBench run
is evidence for the OperateBench Lifecycle Track.


